ABA Mitigation:
In native systems (C++/Rust), the ABA problem occurs if node A is popped, memory freed, and re-allocated at the same pointer address while another thread is executing CAS. Standard solutions include:
1. Tagged pointers (storing a 64-bit monotonically increasing version tag alongside pointer, using DCAS / CMPXCHG16B).
2. Hazard Pointers / Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR) to defer memory deallocation until no active thread holds a reference.

